<title>UK: UK's Blair promises action on missold pensions.</title>
<headline>UK's Blair promises action on missold pensions.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Prime Minister Tony Blair promised action on Wednesday to compensate up to 600,000 Britons who were missold personal pensions under the previous Conservative government.</p>
<p>&quot;It has been an absolute scandal. It is one that we are determined to put right,&quot; Blair told parliament at question time. Treasury minister Helen Liddell had already ordered pension providers to take action, he noted.</p>
<p>&quot;This is a problem that we are looking at urgently. We have acted on it with considerable speed since coming to power and we will act upon it further just as soon as we can,&quot; Blair said.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom 44-171-542 7767</p>
</text>
